The fermionic operator $a_{i}^{\dagger }a_{j}^{\dagger }a_{k}a_{l}$ expands
in terms of Majorana operators as

\begin{align*}
a_{i}^{\dagger }a_{j}^{\dagger }a_{k}a_{l}& =\frac{1}{16}\left\{ \gamma
_{j}\gamma _{k}\gamma _{l}\gamma _{m}+i\gamma _{j}\gamma _{k}\gamma
_{l}\gamma _{m+r}-i\gamma _{j}\gamma _{k}\gamma _{l+r}\gamma _{m}+\gamma
_{j}\gamma _{k}\gamma _{l+r}\gamma _{m+r}\right.  \\
+i& \gamma _{j}\gamma _{k+r}\gamma _{l}\gamma _{m}-\gamma _{j}\gamma
_{k+r}\gamma _{l}\gamma _{m+r}+\gamma _{j}\gamma _{k+r}\gamma _{l+r}\gamma
_{m}+i\gamma _{j}\gamma _{k+r}\gamma _{l+r}\gamma _{m+r} \\
-i& \gamma _{j+r}\gamma _{k}\gamma _{l}\gamma _{m}+\gamma _{j+r}\gamma
_{k}\gamma _{l}\gamma _{m+r}-\gamma _{j+r}\gamma _{k}\gamma _{l+r}\gamma
_{m}-i\gamma _{j+r}\gamma _{k}\gamma _{l+r}\gamma _{m+r} \\
& +\left. \gamma _{j+r}\gamma _{k+r}\gamma _{l}\gamma _{m}+i\gamma
_{j+r}\gamma _{k+r}\gamma _{l}\gamma _{m+r}-i\gamma _{j+r}\gamma
_{k+r}\gamma _{l+r}\gamma _{m}+\gamma _{j+r}\gamma _{k+r}\gamma _{l+r}\gamma
_{m+r}\right\} 
\end{align*}

where $\gamma _{\mu }$ are Majorana operators satisfying $\{\gamma _{\mu
},\gamma _{\nu }\}=2\delta _{\mu \nu }$, with the fermionic mapping 
\begin{align*}
a_{j}& =\tfrac{1}{2}(\gamma _{j}+i\gamma _{j+r}) \\
a_{j}^{\dagger }& =\tfrac{1}{2}(\gamma _{j}-i\gamma _{j+r})
\end{align*}

